{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825258085,"sessionID":"ses_f462b5375ffe0Xe1Ogn1j4dMvc","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e5eab6001wwZhcP6hcj3yHA_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f462b5375ffe0Xe1Ogn1j4dMvc","messageID":"msg_0b9e5eab6001wwZhcP6hcj3yHA","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and all programmatic checks pass. Here's the final verification summary, then the deliverable report.\n\n**Saved:** `extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx` (85 KB)\n- **Deal ledger** – 57 rows × 39 columns (14 visible + collapsed expandable groups), filters, frozen panes, 15 drop-down lists, internal links to Source text, red-bold correction highlighting vs AI original.\n- **Summary**, **Questions**, **Source text** visible; **AI original** and **Lists** hidden.\n\n**Checks run by code:** 92/92 evidence quotations found in the cited passages; 0 structure problems (unique Row ids, non-decreasing Working dates, valid Date basis/method pairs, one Round finality per round, inferred rows tagged, deadline treatments set); AI original matches delivered values exactly; Summary formulas replicate to NDA = 26, contacts = 30, round-bidder units = 9/6/4, inferred exits = 17. Not run: spreadsheet recalculation, link click-through and conditional-format exercise — LibreOffice crashes in this environment on any workbook; formulas were validated only by replicating their criteria against the ledger data.\n\n---\n\n## The sale, in plain terms\n\nIn Q4 2015 Class I rail partner \"Party A\" floated an equity/JV interest in Providence & Worcester, prompting a banker search and GHF's 01/27/2016 engagement (its business was later acquired by BMO). On 03/14/2016 the Board approved a change-in-control process; the week-of-March-28 outreach wave and spring NDAs produced nine non-binding IOIs (05/19–06/01/2016, $17.93–$26.50 as-converted), then six LOIs in late July ($19.20–$24.00). Party B ($24.00) and G&W ($21.15, later $22.15, including a $1.13 South Quay CVR) were chosen as finalists on 07/27/2016; Parties D and E briefly re-entered on 08/01 and were out again by 08/02. With the target ready to sign with Party B, G&W returned on 08/12/2016 with an all-cash $25.00 offer (CVR dropped); Party B declined to improve, the Board called G&W's bid superior, and the merger agreement was signed that day, announced 08/15/2016. Closing was expected in Q4 2016 but is not observed in this filing.\n\n## Most consequential review items (recommendations in Questions)\n\n- **Q1 Round map** – one process, R1 anchored on the week-of-March-28 outreach wave (rejected candidates kept as R004/R005), R2 opening 06/01/2016 and R3 opening 07/27/2016 (Inferred final); no go-shop or post-signing rival.\n- **Q3 NDA/population bases** – 25 wave signers + late entrant Party C = 26, against the filing's \"25\"; two additional Class I rail approaches and Party B's membership in the 11 are unresolved (Counts left blank).\n- **Q4 Inferred closings** – 16 residual non-submitters at the IOI deadline, Party A's Count-0 identity row, Party E's silent close at signing; D's \"at that time\" wording read as Withdrew (alternative flagged).\n- **Q5 Formality/conditions** – Party E's issues-summary LOI kept Informal (borderline); G&W's 08/12 bid Light (alternative None); Party B's 08/04 returned draft recorded as the flagged late reconfirmation.\n- **Q7 Working dates** – display conventions (Q4-2015 midpoints, 04/09 NDA midpoint, five undated LOIs at the 07/20 deadline placed ahead of G&W's 07/21 LOI).\n\nChecks 1, 2, 5 and 8 are **Qualified** (source limitations and untested spreadsheet features are preserved, not resolved); checks 3, 4, 6, 7 pass on the delivered version. This is an AI first pass and has not been human-approved.","time":{"start":1789825247938,"end":1789825258085}}}
